# Review routing. GitHub requests a review from the LAST matching pattern, so
# order is specificity ascending: the catch-all first, the load-bearing seams
# last.
#
# This repository has one maintainer today, so every line resolves to the same
# handle and none of them gate anything by themselves. That is deliberate and it
# is not decoration: the file's job here is to make the OWNERSHIP BOUNDARIES
# explicit and reviewable, so that adding a second maintainer is one handle
# edited per area rather than an argument about where the areas are. The
# boundaries below are the ones the architecture already enforces (CLAUDE.md
# §Architecture, README.md §Architecture) — they are not invented for this file.
#
# To make these binding, enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch
# protection rule for `master`, alongside the required checks
# (Format / test / Consumer clients / Ship inventory + doc-sync / Test harness
# gates / Dependency audit).

# Everything, unless something more specific claims it.
*                                   @xkazm04

# --- the load-bearing seams --------------------------------------------------

# The traits every other crate plugs into. A change here is a change to every
# app and every engine at once: ScrapeApp, the engine traits, the tiered
# Fetcher, Storage (the SQLite job queue), Datasets, the Governor, config.
/crates/core/                       @xkazm04

# The wiring layer. The one crate allowed to depend on everything — routes, the
# worker pool, the scheduler, webhooks, triggers, SSE, datahub.
/crates/server/                     @xkazm04

# The engines. Each depends only on `core`; a change that makes one depend on
# another, or on an app, breaks the dependency rule this repo is built on.
/crates/engine-http/                @xkazm04
/crates/engine-browser/             @xkazm04
/crates/engine-claude/              @xkazm04
/crates/engine-wasm/                @xkazm04
/crates/engine-search/              @xkazm04
/crates/engine-archive/             @xkazm04
/crates/engine-remote/              @xkazm04

# The apps. Self-contained by contract — an app depends only on `core` plus
# parsing libs, never on another app or on an engine crate. The `*-common`
# crates are the ONE exception (shared helpers within a family), which is
# exactly why they are worth routing separately from the apps that use them.
/crates/apps/                       @xkazm04
/crates/apps/grants-common/         @xkazm04
/crates/apps/census-common/         @xkazm04
/crates/apps/trades-common/         @xkazm04

# --- the contracts that reach outside this repo ------------------------------

# The published consumer plane. `openapi.json` is generated from the router and
# pinned to it by a cargo test; every client's wire types are generated from
# that document and diffed in CI. A hand edit here is drift by construction.
/clients/                           @xkazm04
/clients/openapi.json               @xkazm04
/scripts/gen/                       @xkazm04

# The machine-readable pipeline registry. Every app must have a `[[source]]`
# entry (ONBOARDING.md §10).
/catalog/                           @xkazm04

# --- the gates themselves ----------------------------------------------------

# Supply chain and CI. A change here changes what every other change is checked
# against, so it is the one area where a second reviewer buys the most.
/.github/                           @xkazm04
/deny.toml                          @xkazm04
/Cargo.lock                         @xkazm04
/rust-toolchain.toml                @xkazm04
/SECURITY.md                        @xkazm04

# The task runner and the local guardrails. `justfile` is the canonical
# definition of what CI runs; `.githooks/` is what runs before it.
/justfile                           @xkazm04
/.githooks/                         @xkazm04
/scripts/ci/                        @xkazm04

# The agent-facing contract. `.ai/manifest.yaml` nominates the canonical
# guidance file; the two CLAUDE.md files are that guidance.
/.ai/                               @xkazm04
/CLAUDE.md                          @xkazm04
/.claude/CLAUDE.md                  @xkazm04
/docs/features/                     @xkazm04
